// XChaCha20, draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03:
// https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03
//
// ChaCha20 with a twenty-four byte nonce, which it gets by deriving a fresh key
// from the first sixteen bytes of that nonce and then running ordinary ChaCha20
// under it with the remaining eight. The derivation is HChaCha20, the same
// twenty rounds stopped before the feed-forward, so the output looks like a key
// rather than keystream.
//
// The point is not more security per block but a nonce large enough to pick at
// random: twenty-four bytes means a system can generate a nonce per message from
// a good random source and never coordinate, where eight or twelve bytes forces
// a counter and therefore state.
import {
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/spec",
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/cipher/chacha20",
}

import {
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/cipher/chacha20",
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/cipher/xchacha20",
  "moonbitstack/moonbase/base16",
} for "test"
